WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.970
A row of machines, all
modern in the 1890s:

2
00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:08.220
a typewriter, a wax-cylinder
phonograph, a telegraph key,

3
00:00:08.270 --> 00:00:11.810
a railway timetable, a transfusion kit.

4
00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:16.350
Opposite, an old oak table:
a candle, a crucifix,

5
00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:19.490
garlic flowers, a wooden stake.

6
00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:22.290
In the castle, Harker writes in shorthand,

7
00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:27.020
proud that it is "nineteenth century
up-to-date with a vengeance".

8
00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:29.690
A shadow moves between the two tables.

9
00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:33.140
So can 1890s science beat him?

10
00:00:33.190 --> 00:00:36.600
In this mission, you'll unpack
the hunters' modern toolkit:

11
00:00:36.650 --> 00:00:39.280
records, movement and medicine.

12
00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:43.200
You'll see what Harker writes next,
straight after that proud line.

13
00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:46.820
And you'll meet the 1890s
idea of the "criminal type",

14
00:00:46.870 --> 00:00:48.700
and test it on the Count.

15
00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:52.850
Your mission: decide whether
1890s science can beat him.
